    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pănaetōlĭum</span></b> ,
			i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παναιτώλιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the council of the whole of Ætolia</i>,
				<i>a general assembly</i> or <i>congress of the Ætolians</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concilium Aetolorum quod Panaetolium vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					31, 29, 1</span></i>
			; Weissenb. ad <i><span class="en">Liv. 31, 32,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A very high mountain in Ætolia</i>, now
				<i>Viena</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3,
				§ 6</span></i>.</div>
